# Build outputs
*.bin
# ...but SOURCE .bin data must be tracked. `*.bin` above is aimed at ROMs and
# build artifacts; the editor/collision blobs the generators CONSUME are inputs.
# Most were force-added silently over time, which is how the one below got missed:
# tools lens sweep D2 found that the entire level re-bake path hangs off
# ojz_tiles.bin, present on the authoring checkout and carried by nothing, so
# `tools/regenerate-level.sh` could not run in any fresh clone or worktree — and
# the STRESS_ART=1 build shape was dead with it. Negate explicitly rather than
# force-add, so the intent is visible the next time someone reads this file.
!games/sonic4/data/editor/ojz_tiles.bin
# The BG library bodies Aurora writes IN PLACE into this tree (2026-08-30). These are
# NOT derived: Aurora keeps no library store of its own — its only userData file is a
# list of recent project PATHS — so it is a lens on this filesystem and cannot re-export
# them. Untracked, they existed on one disk with no history. Deliberately scoped to the
# authored bodies and their tile blobs; the `.pre-*-backup/`, `.reset-backup-*/` and
# `export/` trees stay ignored, being supersedable or regenerable.
!games/sonic4/data/editor/ojz_bg_*.bin
!games/sonic4/data/editor/ojz_act1_bg*.bin
*.lst
# ...but the s4budget test fixtures ARE listings, on purpose. They are excerpts
# cut from real `sigil build --emit-lst` output (tools/fixtures/make_listing_excerpt.py)
# rather than hand-authored, because a hand-authored listing fixture is how
# test_s4budget stayed green for months against a parser that read nothing
# (tools lens sweep D7). Negated explicitly, not force-added.
!tools/fixtures/*.lst
*.log
*.p
*.h

# seam-1: the resident sound blob + its symbol contract are GENERATED each build
# by `sigil emit_sound_blob` (the .emp native link → the inputs asl packs). Build
# artifacts, regenerated by build.sh — never committed (like the ROMs).
engine/sound/generated/

# Allow test art data
!test/*.bin
# The ring art blobs (compose_ring.py outputs; ring_art.bin was force-added before this rule)
!games/sonic4/test/ring_art.bin
!games/sonic4/test/ring_sparkle_art.bin

# Allow sprite art and DPLC data
!art/uncompressed/**/*.bin
!art/optimized/**/*.bin
!games/sonic4/data/dplc/*.bin
!games/sonic4/data/replays/*.bin
!games/sonic4/data/dplc/optimized/*.bin
!games/sonic4/data/mappings/*.bin
!art/palettes/*.bin
# Donor ANIMATION references — raw reference scripts, embedded by a `const` and
# NEVER by a `pub data`, so they cost zero ROM bytes and exist only so a comptime
# gate can COMPUTE its expectation from the reference instead of restating it.
# (insta_shield_donor_anim.bin is the first; tools/compose_instashield.py emits it.)
!games/sonic4/data/animations/*.bin

# Sound-migration T2: committed --emit-bin twins of the MT/HCZ2 stream .asm
# (mirrors the committed generated .asm — sigil's mt_bank.emp embeds these
# directly; the emitters need external inputs (Zyrinx B&R ROM, skdisasm) so
# they can't run in prebuild). Verified byte-identical to their dc.b .asm
# twins via tools/verify_emit_bin.py before committing.
!games/sonic4/data/sound/song_movingtrucks.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/movingtrucks_pitchtable_stream.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/movingtrucks_patches.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/song_drumtest.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/song_hcz2.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/hcz2_patches.bin

# Sound-migration T3: committed --emit-bin twins of the 9 SFX blob/patch .asm
# (sigil's sfx_bank.emp embeds these directly; two patch banks are zero-byte —
# sfx_36/sfx_62 are PSG-only). Verified byte-identical to their dc.b .asm twins
# via tools/verify_emit_bin.py before committing.
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_33.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_33_patches.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_34.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_34_patches.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_35.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_35_patches.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_36.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_36_patches.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_3C.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_3C_patches.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_62.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_62_patches.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_AB.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_AB_patches.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_B6.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_B6_patches.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_B9.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_B9_patches.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_BA.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_BA_patches.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_BB.bin
!games/sonic4/data/sound/sfx/sfx_BB_patches.bin

# Vendored salvador (ZX0 packer) — keep sources, ignore build artifacts
!tools/salvador/**/*.h
tools/salvador/obj/
tools/salvador/salvador
tools/bin/

# MCP config (machine-specific)
.mcp.json

# ctags symbol index (generated)
tags
*.s4lz
*.zx0
*.tf
__pycache__/
.worktrees/
engine/debug/generated/

# level-gen parcel: the OJZ generated level tree + collision tables ship as
# COMMITTED artifacts (the sound-migration model — reproducible-by-tracking).
# The generators (ojz_strip_gen / ojz_block_gen / ojz_entity_gen /
# import_sk_collision) read out-of-repo donor projects (sonic_hack / skdisasm),
# so they cannot run in the build; re-bake is MANUAL (tools/regenerate-level.sh).
# A fresh checkout builds from these tracked bytes with no seed step.
!games/sonic4/data/generated/**/*.asm
!games/sonic4/data/generated/**/*.emp
!games/sonic4/data/generated/**/*.bin
!games/sonic4/data/generated/**/*.zx0
!games/sonic4/data/collision/**/*.bin
# The editor working data the re-bake consumes (painted section nametables +
# per-section collision); the `section_*` globs never cross `/`, so the
# .*-backup/ dirs and dead timestamped bg experiments stay ignored.
!games/sonic4/data/editor/ojz/act1/section_*.tiles.bin
!games/sonic4/data/editor/ojz/act1/section_*.coll.bin

# The background layout the project NAMES. `ojz_bglib.json` is tracked and
# `ojz/act1/section_0.meta.json` binds `bgLayoutRef` to this id — so without the
# negation a clean clone carries the manifest and the binding and NOT the picture,
# and the editor silently authors against the act default instead of the background
# the repo says it uses. That is the `*.bin` blanket two rules up catching source
# data again, which is the exact case the comment there already records for
# ojz_tiles.bin, with the same remedy: negate explicitly.
# Scoped to the REFERENCED layout only. The other sixteen (deep-forest-v1..v16) are
# the owner's experiments and whether they are dead is his call, not this lane's —
# parked as a question rather than resolved by a wildcard.
!games/sonic4/data/editor/ojz_bg_ingame-forest-v15-1786630615596.bin
!games/sonic4/data/editor/ojz_bg_ingame-forest-v15-1786630615596_tiles.bin
!games/sonic4/data/editor/ojz/act1/section_*.collattr.bin
!games/sonic4/data/editor/ojz/act1/section_*.collattrb.bin
!games/sonic4/data/editor/ojz/chunks_tiles.bin
# ...but NOT the editor's `export/` dump. Aurora still emits its legacy `.asm`
# export there (act_descriptor / entity_data / vram_bases). Those exact three
# files were DELETED by Parcel J (46c2e0f0, 2026-08-01) on an owner pre-ruling,
# with an unwired-proof: no build file, sigil test or tool reads the path, and
# all 47 `ojz_*` labels they define are referenced only within the dir. The
# editor re-emitted them on 2026-08-12 and they have been untracked noise since.
# `tools/level_staleness.py` already excludes the directory BY NAME (SKIP_DIR_NAMES,
# covered by test_export_dir_is_excluded), so ignoring it changes no build behaviour.
games/sonic4/data/editor/ojz/act1/export/

# Emulator save-states written beside the ROM at the repo root (Oracle's "ONSS"
# format, ~870 KB each). Ephemeral and specific to one ROM build — like the ROMs
# themselves, never committed. Root-anchored so a deliberately tracked `*.state*`
# fixture deeper in the tree would still be possible.
/*.state*

# Build tool caches (content-hash keyed)
tools/.cache/
*.wav

# Scratch VGM register captures (root-level only). Intentional reference
# captures live under docs/research/reference_captures/ and stay tracked.
/*.vgm
# reference disassembly blobs + captures are research artifacts, not build output
!docs/research/z80_blobs/**
!docs/research/reference_captures/*.vgm

# Third-party reference repos cloned for research (upstream, not vendored)
docs/research/external/

# staged S3K character extraction (design #3 prep) — data, not build output
!games/sonic4/data/characters_staging/**/*.bin
